; The ONE variable: `layout_direction = 3` on a default (LEFT) icon-mode
; ItemList. Godot mirrors each row's icon inside the list's OWN width
; (item_list.cpp:1582-1584), then moves the label to its own RTL pen,
; `size.width - rect.width + icon.width - text_ofs.x + h_separation`
; (:1664-1667), and right-aligns it in its box (:1668). That pen is NOT the
; mirror of the LTR one, so the label sits a different distance from its icon
; in each direction and a plain mirror reads wrong. Both lists are the same
; width and hold the same two rows, of deliberately different widths, so only
; the direction can move either piece. unit-item-list-guide-lines.tscn is the
; only other LEFT-mode ItemList and it is LTR with no icon at all, so a
; regression in either branch is invisible everywhere else.

